      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win the pot by having the highest-ranking hand at showdown, or by being the last player standing when all others have folded.',
      'Turn-flow example: Ante; optional blind (buio, controbuio, over) before deal. Deal 5 cards each. First betting round: pass or open (with pair of Jacks or better, or 4-card straight-flush draw); then fold, call, raise. Draw: each surviving player may exchange 0–4 cards. Second betting round: bet, check, or parol (throw in and carry pot); then fold, call, raise. Showdown: highest hand wins; flush beats full house; straight flush has min/medium/max with min beating max.',
      'Scoring example: Pot is won by the player with the highest-ranking hand at showdown, or by the last player left when all others fold. Three-way straight flush (min, medium, max) splits the pot. Highest-ranking hand at showdown wins the pot; or the last player standing when all others have folded..',
